<p>"Hero + supporting" KPI indicator. <strong>One headline metric on the left</strong> (huge value, delta + period + target meta row, big sparkline) — the marketing/exec story you want at a glance. <strong>A vertical side rail of supporting metrics on the right</strong> (compact tiles, each with label · value · delta-vs-prev). Card-level container query collapses the side-by-side layout to stacked when the card narrows below 700px so the same markup works in narrow page-grid cells.</p>

<style>
/* === Card chrome === */
.kpi-hero-list {
  container-type: inline-size;
}
.kpi-hero-list__header {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 1.6rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}
.kpi-hero-list__live {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  color: var(--pa-text-secondary);
}
.kpi-hero-list__livedot {
  width: 0.8rem;
  height: 0.8rem;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--pa-positive);
  box-shadow: 0 0 6px var(--pa-positive);
  animation: kpiPulse 1.6s ease-in-out infinite;
}
@keyframes kpiPulse { 50% { opacity: 0.35; } }

.kpi-hero-list__body { padding: 1.6rem; }

/* === Two-column layout: hero left, side rail right.
       Stacks vertically when the card is narrower than 700px. The hero
       eats more horizontal space at wide widths because the big value
       wants room to breathe; at narrow widths the columns are equal. === */
.kpi-hero-list__layout {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  gap: 1.4rem;
}
@container (max-width: 700px) {
  .kpi-hero-list__layout {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}

.kpi-hero-list__rail {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 1rem;
}

/* === HERO panel (left): label · big value · meta row · sparkline === */
.kpi-hero-main {
  position: relative;
  padding: 1.8rem 2rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--pa-border-color);
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  /* Sentiment colour cascades to the chart and any deltas via currentColor.
     Override per-tile via the .kpi-hero-main--positive/negative/etc modifiers. */
  --kpi-hero-color: var(--pa-positive);
}
.kpi-hero-main--positive { --kpi-hero-color: var(--pa-positive); }
.kpi-hero-main--negative { --kpi-hero-color: var(--pa-negative); }
.kpi-hero-main--neutral  { --kpi-hero-color: var(--pa-neutral); }
.kpi-hero-main--up-strong { --kpi-hero-color: var(--pa-very-positive); }

.kpi-hero-main__label {
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.4rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pa-text-color-1) 60%, transparent);
}

.kpi-hero-main__value {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  line-height: 1;
  margin: 0.4rem 0 0.6rem;
}
.kpi-hero-main__num {
  /* Container-query-relative — scales with the hero panel's width. Floor
     keeps it readable in narrow page-grid cards; ceiling caps it on
     ultra-wide canonicals. */
  font-size: clamp(4rem, 17cqi, 7rem);
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  color: var(--pa-text-color-1);
}
.kpi-hero-main__unit {
  font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 8cqi, 3rem);
  font-weight: 500;
  color: var(--pa-text-secondary);
  margin: 0 0.1rem;
}

/* Meta row under the big value: inline delta (arrow + %), period text,
   target — all on one baseline. 3 columns; the period column takes the
   remaining space and wraps if needed at narrow widths. */
.kpi-hero-main__meta {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 0.4rem 1.4rem;
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.3rem;
}
.kpi-hero-main__delta {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 0.4rem;
  color: var(--kpi-hero-color);
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  line-height: 1.2;
}
.kpi-hero-main__period {
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pa-text-color-1) 60%, transparent);
  line-height: 1.3;
}
.kpi-hero-main__target {
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pa-text-color-1) 50%, transparent);
  text-align: end;
}

/* Hero sparkline — fixed-height SVG pinned to the bottom of a flex-grow
   container. Chart container expands to fill any leftover vertical space
   in the hero column (when the side rail forces a tall grid row); the
   SVG inside stays at a fixed pixel height, so the line shape is never
   distorted along the Y axis no matter how tall the parent gets. Same
   reason the trailing dot is an HTML span instead of an SVG circle —
   preserveAspectRatio="none" stretches everything inside the SVG, so
   anything that should keep its shape needs to live outside that scaling
   or have its dimensions in absolute pixels. */
.kpi-hero-main__chart {
  flex: 1 1 10rem;
  min-height: 10rem;
  margin-top: 0.6rem;
  color: var(--kpi-hero-color);
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-end;     /* SVG wrap pinned to the bottom; extra space appears above */
}
/* Wrapper at fixed height — the SVG, the JS-appended dot, and any other
   chart inhabitants all live in here and inherit its dimensions. */
.kpi-hero-main__chart-svg {
  position: relative;
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: var(--pa-chart-trendline-height);
}
.kpi-hero-main__chart-svg svg {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  overflow: visible;
}
.kpi-hero-main__chart polyline {
  fill: none;
  stroke: currentColor;
  stroke-width: var(--pa-chart-trendline-stroke);
  stroke-linecap: round;
  stroke-linejoin: round;
}
.kpi-hero-main__chart polygon {
  fill: currentColor;
  fill-opacity: 0.18;
  stroke: none;
}

/* === SIDE rail tile ===
   2×2 grid where the value spans both rows on the right column. Left column
   has label (row 1) and delta (row 2) stacked. Value is vertically centred
   across the whole tile height — feels balanced when the label is one line,
   and still reads cleanly when the label wraps to two lines. */
.kpi-hero-side {
  position: relative;
  padding: 1.2rem 1.4rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--pa-border-color);
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
  grid-template-areas:
    "label  value"
    "delta  value";
  column-gap: 1.2rem;
  row-gap: 0.4rem;
  align-items: center;
  --kpi-side-color: var(--pa-positive);
}
.kpi-hero-side--positive { --kpi-side-color: var(--pa-positive); }
.kpi-hero-side--negative { --kpi-side-color: var(--pa-negative); }
.kpi-hero-side--neutral  { --kpi-side-color: var(--pa-neutral); }
.kpi-hero-side--up-strong { --kpi-side-color: var(--pa-very-positive); }

.kpi-hero-side__label {
  grid-area: label;
  align-self: end;        /* sit at bottom of row 1 — tucks against the centred value */
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.3rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pa-text-color-1) 60%, transparent);
  line-height: 1.25;
}
.kpi-hero-side__value {
  grid-area: value;
  align-self: center;     /* vertically centred across the spanned rows */
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  line-height: 1;
  white-space: nowrap;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: baseline;
}
.kpi-hero-side__num {
  font-size: 2.4rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  color: var(--pa-text-color-1);
}
.kpi-hero-side__unit {
  font-size: 1.5rem;        /* bumped from 1.2rem so the unit reads more clearly next to the bigger num */
  font-weight: 500;
  color: var(--pa-text-secondary);
  margin: 0 0.35rem;        /* visible gap between value and unit (was 0.1rem — felt glued together) */
}
.kpi-hero-side__delta {
  grid-area: delta;
  align-self: start;      /* sit at top of row 2 — tucks against the centred value */
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--kpi-side-color);
}

/* === Footer caption === */
.kpi-hero-list__footer {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 1rem;
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: var(--pa-text-secondary);
}
.kpi-hero-list__footer strong {
  color: var(--pa-text-color-1);
  font-weight: 700;
}

/* === Hover detail popover (cursor-anchored, same recipe as elsewhere) === */
.kpi-hero-detail {
  position: fixed;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  visibility: hidden;
  pointer-events: none;
  z-index: 9000;
  min-width: 26rem;
  max-width: 32rem;
  background: var(--pa-detail-bg);
  color: var(--pa-detail-text);
  padding: 1.2rem 1.5rem;
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.25rem;
  line-height: 1.5;
  border-radius: 0.4rem;
  box-shadow: var(--pa-detail-shadow);
}
.kpi-hero-detail[data-show] { visibility: visible; }
.kpi-hero-detail-title {
  text-transform: uppercase;
